  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I've added $5.60 in credit to your account for order Q-7201. You can use it on a future order. Late deliveries are compensated with account credit, not refunds to your card.\n\nI'm sorry the order came so late and the app showed it as delivered when it wasn't. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I appreciate the apology, but $5.60 in credit doesn't really cover it. The app said it was delivered around 7 and I was sitting at home waiting until 7:45. My order number is 7201, not Q-7201, so you might want to check that's the right order."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Order Q-7201 is the right one. It's the Burger Barn order you placed at 6:15 PM today for $36.59, and it's the only recent order on your account. The \"7201\" you gave is the number part of that ID.\n\nI understand $5.60 feels small after waiting that long. But I can't go beyond what the policy sets for a delivery that's 47 minutes late, and that's 20% of the food subtotal as account credit. I can't add goodwill credits or card refunds for lateness. The wrong \"delivered\" status doesn't change the amount either. I used the actual handoff time at 7:47 PM, not the app's 6:58 PM mark.\n\nIf you'd like a person to review this, I can pass it to a specialist, who would follow up within 24 hours. I can't promise what they'd decide. Would you like me to do that?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I'm not interested in more credit I can't use on a dinner I already paid for. Yes, pass it to a specialist. I'd like someone to actually look at why the app said it was delivered when nothing had arrived. My number is 415-555-0232 if they need to reach me."
  },
  {
   "role": "tool",
   "name": "escalate_to_human",
   "args": {
    "customer_id": "D202",
    "order_id": "Q-7201",
    "reason": "customer_request",
    "summary": "Customer Leo Brandt asked to speak to a person. Order Q-7201 (Burger Barn) was promised 19:00. Courier app marked it delivered at 18:58, 2.1 miles from the address. The actual in-person handoff was at 19:47, 47 minutes late. I issued the standard late credit of $5.60 (20% of the $28 subtotal). The customer is unhappy with the amount and wants someone to investigate why the app showed delivered when nothing had arrived. Phone: 415-555-0232."
   },
   "result": {
    "escalation_id": "ESC-700",
